# s4-engine-approval: core wiring (applied by the lead after the wave)

[cargo: native/core/crates/mixdog-browser-engine/Cargo.toml, section [dependencies], after the `mixdog-browser-policy` line]
mixdog-core-base = { workspace = true }   # approval/requester.rs: rooms::ids (own_bot_of_session: home and room-member session ids)
mixdog-js = { workspace = true }          # approval/classify.rs (JsRegex POST_CONTROL_NAME) and binding.rs (nodepath::is_absolute_host)
sha2 = { workspace = true }               # approval/binding.rs command_hash (Sha256)
url = { workspace = true }                # approval/classify.rs origin_of_url

# Edges checked: no crate in native/core depends on mixdog-browser-engine except its own Cargo.toml, so mixdog-core-base
# cannot close a cycle. mixdog-workspace-hack is regenerated by the lead's hakari step as usual.

[compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING]
no change: this task registers no protocol service.

[consumers, for s4-tool-adapter and the actions tasks]
- ApprovalPort::ask(BrowserApprovalPrompt) is called with `classify(...).prompt`; a Deny answer becomes
  `ApprovalError::NotApproved{reason}` through `binding::verify`.
- Every host request of the approved step carries `expect: binding::precondition(&ask.binding)`; an upload also sends
  `receiver_key` from the same binding. The host answers -32010 when the document, URL or origin moved.
- The caller of `approval::plan` supplies `ActionPolicy::from_env(MIXDOG_BROWSER_CONFIRM_ACTIONS, MIXDOG_BROWSER_DENY_ACTIONS,
  MIXDOG_BROWSER_CONFIRM_SUBMIT, is_action)` where `is_action` is the registry's rule for a Browser Use action name.
- The gate (not the engine) decides standing allow, unattended runs, "Allow all actions" and session grants, using
  `requester::own_bot_of_session`, `requester::resolve_requester`, `requester::approval_surface_session_id` and
  `binding::mark_outside` (card `outside` flags). A payment prompt (`prompt.payment`) is never covered by any allow.
